\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Sequoia Capital also led a $56 million funding round for Astrocade, announced May 5, 2026, a startup enabling non-technical users to create playable games using generative AI tools. Astrocade aims to make game creation a mainstream consumer activity, using AI to generate playable game logic, art assets, and mechanics from simple text descriptions. Sequoia's investment reflects confidence in the platform's potential to integrate both game creation and gameplay within a single ecosystem, a differentiation from prior tools that produced content for external platforms. The company faces the dual challenge of ensuring retention and quality, as generating functional games quickly does not guarantee a sustained and engaging player experience. The platform's long-term success will depend on its ability to implement effective curation and iteration systems while establishing an ecosystem comparable in scale and community engagement to existing platforms.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Accel has been similarly active, with its India-focused operations anchoring several significant funding rounds. On June 30, 2026, franchise-driven omnichannel grocery and FMCG chain Apna Mart announced a \u8377 120 crore (approximately $12.7 million) Series C round co-led by Accel India and Fundamentum, with additional support from Peak XV Partners. The round marks Apna Mart's second funding event in just over a year, following a $25 million Series B in March 2025 also led by Fundamentum and Accel. Regulatory filings indicate the company's board approved the issuance of 2,367 Series C compulsorily convertible preference shares at \u8377 5,06,757 each, with Accel India and Fundamentum each committing \u8377 55 crore and Peak XV Partners contributing \u8377 10 crore. Apna Mart's valuation is projected to reach approximately \u8377 1,470 crore, nearly double the \u8377 738 crore recorded at its last funding round. Founded by Abhishek Singh and Chetan Garg, the company operates a franchise-led quick commerce model targeting Tier II and Tier III cities, reporting operating revenue of \u8377 185 crore in fiscal year ending March 2025 and claiming revenue growth of 2.5 times to \u8377 500 crore in FY26.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 On June 29, 2026, Accel India led a Rs 130 crore Series A round for Bengaluru-based credit management startup Oolka, valuing the company at approximately Rs 730 crore. Accel India invested Rs 87.22 crore in the round, with Lightspeed contributing Rs 20.87 crore and Z47 \u8212  formerly Matrix Partners \u8212  adding Rs 20.86 crore. Meesho co-founders Vidit Aatrey and Sanjeev Barnwal each participated with investments of Rs 32.65 lakh. Founded in 2024 by Utkrishta Kumar, Oolka is developing an AI-powered credit management platform designed to help users track, manage, and improve credit health. A prior $7 million seed round supported the company's growth to nearly 2 million users and over Rs 100 crore in processed credit repayments, with banking partnerships including Yes Bank, IDFC First Bank, and AU Small Finance Bank. Oolka reported modest revenue of Rs 5.52 lakh against a loss of Rs 5.58 crore in FY25 and has not yet submitted its FY26 results, competing against platforms including GoodScore, OneScore, Paisabazaar, and CRED.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Also on June 29, 2026, Accel backed Pocket \u8212  developed by Open Vision Engineering, Inc. \u8212  with an $11 million funding round alongside Y Combinator and individual investors including Guillermo Rauch, Mati Staniszewski, and Kaz Nejatian. Pocket is a dedicated AI hardware device designed to capture conversations and generate concise summaries, speaker-attributed notes, and actionable follow-up items. The company first gained attention following a concept video in late 2024 that generated thousands of pre-orders, subsequently launched in October 2025, and shipped over 10,000 devices on its first day. As of March 2026, Pocket reported an annualized revenue run rate of $27 million and cumulative shipments exceeding 35,000 devices. CEO and co-founder Akshay Narisetti stated the company was founded on the belief that the best }
{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ul\cf2 technology}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0
\ulnone\cf2  should help people be more present, not more distracted. Accel partner Cecilia Wang described Pocket as helping define a new category of AI-native devices, noting the team's combination of product vision and execution as central reasons for the firm's investment, and expressing confidence in the company's path to reaching millions of users and shaping the future of AI hardware.}
